<section style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="id93154af8-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc" identifier="/us/usc/t42/s242c"><num value="242c">§ 242c.</num><heading> Appointment and authority of the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</heading><subsection style="-uslm-lc:I19" class="indent2 firstIndent-2" id="id93154af9-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc" identifier="/us/usc/t42/s242c/a"><num value="a" class="bold">(a)</num><heading class="bold"> In general</heading><content><p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (referred to in this section as the “CDC”) shall be headed by the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (referred to in this section as the “Director”), who shall be appointed by the President, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate. Such individual shall also serve as the Administrator of the Agency for Toxic Substances and Disease Registry consistent with <ref href="/us/usc/t42/s9604/i">section 9604(i) of this title</ref>. The Director shall perform functions provided for in subsection (b
